  "goodToKnow": "Das Verwaltungsgericht is an administrative court, where citizens can challenge decisions by authorities: building permits, school places, asylum decisions, demonstration bans. Germany has specialised court branches: ordinary, administrative, labour, social and tax courts. The highest administrative court is the Bundesverwaltungsgericht in Leipzig, which in 2018 allowed diesel driving bans in cities. Plural: die Verwaltungsgerichte."
